WITH input(src_slug, src_ch, src_v, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'hosea', 1, 10, '*He shall save his people from their sins* maps the Lo-Ammi → sons-of-the-living-Elohim restoration arc onto the naming of Yahusha (Jesus); the *people* he saves is the same people Hosea names.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'jeremiah', 31, 10, '*He that scattered Yashar''el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* — the gathering hand named in Jer 31:10 is the *Yah* in Yahusha''s name.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'ezekiel', 36, 22, '*I do not this for your sakes, O house of Yashar''el (Israel), but for mine holy name''s sake* — the Yah who saves in Matt 1:21 saves for his own name''s sake; the gospel is name-grace, not merit-grace.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'deuteronomy', 9, 5, '*Not for thy righteousness ... but ... that he may perform the word which Yahuah (the LORD) sware unto thy fathers* — the prior-promise structure that the Messiah''s name announces is now being kept.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 1, '2-kings', 17, 6, 'The Magi from the east arrive from territories adjacent to the Assyrian-resettlement zones of the scattered northern tribes — the first beat of the gathering, those near where the scattered seed lived hearing the proclamation that had reached their lands through Daniel''s witness.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 6, 'micah', 5, 2, '*And thou Beth-lehem, in the land of Yahudah (Judah)* — the prophetic localization of the Messianic birth to the seed-line town of David. The gathering centers on the seed-line geography.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 3, 'isaiah', 40, 3, 'The OT prophetic source — the voice in the wilderness preparing the way of Yahuah (the LORD), in the chapter that opens Yeshayahu''s (Isaiah''s) gathering-and-return prophecies (chs. 40-66).'),
  ('matthew', 3, 9, 'hosea', 1, 10, 'The *Elohim (God) is able of these stones to raise up children unto Avraham (Abraham)* read against Hosea''s *in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people, there it shall be said unto them, Ye are the sons of the living Elohim (God)* — the scattered seed in dispersion being recovered as the children of Avraham (Abraham) Yahuah (God) raises up.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 9, 'isaiah', 51, 1, '*Look unto the rock whence ye are hewn ... look unto Avraham (Abraham) your father, and unto Sarah that bare you* — Yeshayahu''s (Isaiah''s) rock-hewn-lineage image; Avraham (Abraham) himself is the *rock,* and Yahuah (God) recovers the seed from the rock.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 10, 'ezekiel', 20, 37, '*I will cause you to pass under the rod ... and I will purge out from among you the rebels* — the post-harvest sifting Yochanan (John) is naming with the *axe is laid unto the root of the trees* image.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 12, 'ezekiel', 20, 38, '*His fan is in his hand, and he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire* — the chaff-from-wheat sifting that Ezek 20:38 names as the rod-purge of the rebels from among the gathered.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 15, 'isaiah', 9, 1, 'The OT prophetic source — the light dawning on the people of Zevulun (Zebulun) and Naphtali, the scattered-northern-tribe-in-darkness in their tribal territory.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 19, 'jeremiah', 16, 14, '*Behold, I will send for many fishers, saith Yahuah (the LORD), and they shall fish them* — the prophetic Jeremiah-16 fishers as the agents of the second-Exodus gathering of the scattered seed; Matthew 4:19''s *fishers of men* is the explicit identification of the disciples with the Jer 16 fishers.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 25, 'ezekiel', 37, 21, '*I will take the children of Yashar''el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land* — the early-ministry geographic-scope summary as the beginning of the Ezek 37 gathering.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 5, 'psalms', 37, 9, '*The meek shall inherit the earth* — the Beatitude is a verbatim quotation of Psalm 37:11; the surrounding context (vv.9-11, 22, 29, 34) is the gathering-and-land-inheritance arc the Beatitude lands on.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 9, 'ezekiel', 36, 23, '*I will sanctify my great name ... when I shall be sanctified in you before their eyes ... For I will take you from among the heathen, and gather you out of all countries* — *Hallowed be thy name* is the gathering-prayer; the Name is sanctified through the gathering of the scattered.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 10, 'daniel', 7, 13, '*Thy kingdom come* — the eschatological-kingdom prayer; the Daniel kingdom-transfer Yahusha (Jesus) refused to short-circuit at Matt 4:8-10.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 10, 'daniel', 2, 44, 'The Elohim-of-heaven kingdom that breaks all the kingdoms of the present age — what the kingdom-citizens pray come.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 9, 'ezekiel', 36, 22, 'The sanctification of the Name is *for mine holy name''s sake* — the grace-from-name''s-sake grammar that the *Hallowed be thy name* prayer presupposes.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 12, 'leviticus', 16, 30, '*For on that day shall the priest make an atonement for you, to cleanse you, that ye may be clean from all your sins before Yahuah (the LORD)* — the Yom Kippur atonement architecture the forgiveness-petition draws on.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'matthew', 18, 32, 'The parable of the unforgiving servant — the king reverses the forgiveness; the framework''s NT illustration of the principle.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'isaiah', 43, 5, '*I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west* — the framework reading of *many shall come from east and west* as the gathering-prophecy of the scattered seed; NOT the Christian inclusion-replacement read.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'psalms', 107, 2, '*Gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south* — the redeemed-from-the-lands directional-formula.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'zechariah', 8, 7, '*I will save my people from the east country, and from the west country* — the gathering-to-Yerushalayim (Jerusalem) directional-formula.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'isaiah', 49, 12, '*Behold, these shall come from far: and, lo, these from the north and from the west; and these from the land of Sinim* — the directional-formula of the gathering.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'isaiah', 11, 11, 'The second-gathering prophecy; *shall assemble the outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth.*'),
  ('matthew', 8, 11, 'ezekiel', 37, 21, '*I will take the children of Yashar''el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone* — the Ezekiel 37 gathering-prophecy companion.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 28, 'joshua', 13, 24, 'The eastern-tribal-inheritance allotment to Gad and the half-tribe of Manasheh (Manasseh) — the territory Yahusha (Jesus) enters at the Gergesene/Gadarene exorcism; the gathering-ministry reaches the eastern tribes'' land.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 36, 'ezekiel', 34, 1, 'The full Tanakh-prophetic-thunder against the false-shepherds.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 36, 'ezekiel', 34, 23, '*I will set up one shepherd over them ... even my servant David.* The Davidic-Messianic shepherd-restoration; Yahusha (Jesus) IS this shepherd; the multitudes have not yet been gathered to him.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 36, 'jeremiah', 50, 6, '*My people hath been lost sheep: their shepherds have caused them to go astray* — the exile-leadership-failure named.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 36, 'numbers', 27, 17, 'The original framing of the phrase from Mosheh''s (Moses''s) succession-prayer.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 37, 'joel', 3, 13, '*Put ye in the sickle, for the harvest is ripe* — the eschatological-harvest Tanakh-anchor.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 37, 'isaiah', 27, 12, '*Ye shall be gathered one by one* — the gathering-of-the-scattered-seed under the harvest-figure.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 23, 'ezekiel', 20, 33, 'The eschatological-gathering-with-sifting the present-age mission-to-Yashar''el (Israel) is moving toward.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 23, 'matthew', 28, 19, 'The mission-scope extending to all-nations-where-the-scattered-seed-are; the gathering continues across the present age.'),
  ('matthew', 12, 18, 'isaiah', 42, 1, 'The direct Tanakh-source.'),
  ('matthew', 12, 21, 'isaiah', 42, 1, 'The Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42 servant-citation read in framework as the scattered-seed-in-the-nations-territories gathering, NOT categorical-extension to the third covenant-category (the nations of Genesis 1, who are not the seed of promise).'),
  ('matthew', 12, 30, 'john', 10, 11, '*He that gathereth not with me scattereth abroad* — the gathering-language ties to the good-shepherd-pericope''s *other sheep I have, which are not of this fold.*'),
  ('matthew', 13, 38, 'ezekiel', 37, 21, '*I will take the children of Yashar''el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land* — the good-seed-of-the-children-of-the-kingdom is the same gathered-remnant the Tanakh-prophets name.'),
  ('matthew', 13, 43, 'daniel', 12, 3, '*They that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament* — the direct Tanakh-anchor for the righteous-shining-as-the-sun.'),
  ('matthew', 14, 13, 'ezekiel', 34, 11, 'The shepherd''s-compassion-and-feeding of the scattered-flock in the Galilee-northern-house''s territories.'),
  ('matthew', 14, 20, 'ezekiel', 37, 21, 'The twelve-baskets-substance signaling the twelve-tribes-restoration-architecture extended.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'matthew', 15, 24, '*His people* in 1:21 is locked by 15:24''s *the lost sheep of the house of Yashar''el (Israel)* — same mission scope at the front door of the gospel as at the Canaanite-woman pericope.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'matthew', 10, 5, 'Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) own missionary instruction to the twelve names the same scope as v.21''s *his people.*'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'ezekiel', 34, 11, 'Yahuah (the LORD) as the shepherd who himself goes out to seek the lost — Yahusha (Jesus) as the *Yah saves* of v.21 is the Ezek 34 shepherd in flesh.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'john', 10, 27, '*My sheep hear my voice* — the hearing is the revealing of who *his people* are; the proclamation is broad, the audience is the scattered citizens.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'matthew', 28, 19, 'The post-resurrection broadcast through the nations does not abolish the first-mission scope; it disperses the proclamation to where the scattered sheep are.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 3, 'genesis', 38, 26, '*She hath been more righteous than I* — Tamar''s case preserves the kingship-tribe line through Yahudah''s (Judah''s) own failure to honor levirate.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 5, 'joshua', 2, 11, 'Rachab''s confession of Yahuah (the LORD) as *Elohim (God) in heaven above, and in earth beneath* — the specific Yah-ordained grafting in her own life.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 5, 'joshua', 6, 25, 'Rachab dwelt in Yashar''el (Israel) *even unto this day* — the grafting is settled, not perpetually open.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 5, 'ruth', 1, 16, '*Thy people shall be my people, and thy Elohim (God) my Elohim (God)* — Ruth''s specific Yah-ordained transfer from the Moavite peripheral-Avrahamic branch into the Yashar''eli (Israelite) covenant body.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 5, 'genesis', 19, 36, 'Moav (Moab) as the son of Lot, Avraham''s (Abraham''s) nephew — locating Ruth''s lineage on the peripheral-Avrahamic branch, not in the unrelated nations.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 5, 'ruth', 4, 14, 'Boaz as kinsman-redeemer — the Tanakh-prefiguring of Yahusha (Jesus) as the kinsman-redeemer of the scattered seed.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 6, '2-samuel', 11, 27, '*The thing that David had done displeased Yahuah (the LORD)* — Matthew''s naming of Bathsheba as *her of Uriah* refuses to whitewash the sin in the kingship line.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 1, 'genesis', 12, 3, '*In thee shall all families of the earth be blessed* — the Avrahamic seed-promise the genealogy traces to the Messiah.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 1, '2-samuel', 7, 12, '*I will set up thy seed after thee ... and I will establish the throne of his kingdom for ever* — the Davidic kingship promise the genealogy traces to the Messiah.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 11, '2-kings', 24, 14, 'The actual deportation of Yahudah (Judah) to Babylon — the historical anchor of Matthew''s hinge.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 11, '2-kings', 17, 6, 'The earlier Assyrian captivity of the northern house — the deportation Matthew implicitly carries because the northern house is still scattered when the genealogy reaches Yahusha (Jesus).'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'jeremiah', 25, 11, 'The seventy years of Babylonian captivity prophesied.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'ezekiel', 37, 15, 'The two-stick prophecy — the joining of the stick of Yahudah (Judah) and the stick of Yosef (Joseph)/Ephraim in the hand of the Messianic David. The Messiah of Matt 1 is the David of Ezek 37.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'ezekiel', 20, 33, 'The wilderness-of-the-peoples gathering — the post-scattering prophetic ingathering that the Messianic mission addresses.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'isaiah', 11, 11, '*He shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* — both houses, named, gathered.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'hosea', 1, 11, '*Then shall the children of Yahudah (Judah) and the children of Yashar''el (Israel) be gathered together, and appoint themselves one head* — the one head Hosea names is the Messiah Matthew is genealogizing.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 17, 'ezra', 2, 1, 'The partial return from Babylon under Zerubbavel (Zerubbabel) — establishing that the post-exilic remnant in the land is not the prophetic ingathering.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'isaiah', 7, 14, 'The Old Testament prophetic source of the *Immanuel* naming; Matthew''s quote is the apostolic apposition.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'john', 1, 14, '*And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us* — the Yochanan (John) parallel to the Matthean *Immanuel.*'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'exodus', 33, 20, '*Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live* — the formless-infinite Father not seen by mortal eyes; the Formed in flesh is what is seen in Matt 1:23.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'john', 1, 18, '*No man hath seen Elohim (God) at any time; the only begotten Son ... he hath declared him* — the Yochannine (Johannine) lock on Exodus 33:20.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'genesis', 18, 1, '*Yahuah (the LORD) appeared unto him in the plains of Mamre ... and, lo, three men stood by him* — a theophany of the Formed in pre-incarnate form, prefiguring the Matt 1:23 incarnation.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, 'exodus', 24, 9, '*They saw the Elohim (God) of Yashar''el (Israel) ... they saw Elohim (God), and did eat and drink* — the seventy elders see the Formed. The Formless is not what is seen; the Formed is.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, '1-corinthians', 15, 28, '*Then shall the Son also himself be subject unto him that put all things under him* — the eternal submission of the Formed to the Formless preserved in the eschaton. The Trinity''s co-equal-persons frame cannot account for the eschatological submission; the framework''s Formless-and-Formed reading carries it natively.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 23, '1-corinthians', 11, 3, '*The head of the Messiah (Christ) is Elohim (God)* — the eternal headship of the Father over the Son, preserved through and after the incarnation.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'numbers', 13, 16, '*And Mosheh (Moses) called Oshea (Hoshea) the son of Nun, Yahoshua (Joshua)* — the Old Testament parent-name to *Yahusha* is *Yahoshua* (the same root, the same divine-name component), and the renaming itself is theological.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'acts', 4, 12, '*Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved* — the name is the announcement and the means.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'psalms', 68, 4, '*Sing unto Elohim (God), sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name Yah, and rejoice before him* — the short form *Yah* preserved in the Old Testament as the explicit object of praise; the *Yah* in *Yahusha* is the name praised here.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'joshua', 1, 1, 'The commissioning of Yahoshua (Joshua) to lead the entry into the land — the first-fruits typology of the Messianic ingathering.'),
  ('matthew', 1, 21, 'philippians', 2, 9, '*Wherefore Elohim (God) also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name* — the apostolic recognition that the name carries the authority.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 1, 'daniel', 2, 48, 'Daniel''s promotion to chief of the wise men of Babylon — the institutional source of the Magi''s prophetic knowledge.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 2, 'numbers', 24, 17, '*There shall come a Star out of Ya''aqov (Jacob), and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar''el (Israel)* — the Balaam prophecy of the Star-and-Sceptre that the Magi recognized.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 2, 'daniel', 9, 24, 'The seventy-weeks prophecy giving the timing of *Messiah the Prince* — the Daniel-tradition Magi would have known the timing window from.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 9, 'exodus', 13, 21, 'The pillar of cloud and fire that led Yashar''el (Israel) in the wilderness — the Tanakh-pattern for the shekinah-leading-by-visible-sign that the Matthew-2 star manifests.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 11, 'isaiah', 60, 6, '*They shall bring gold and incense* — the prophetic specification of the gifts.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 3, 'obadiah', 1, 10, '*For thy violence against thy brother Ya''aqov (Jacob) shame shall cover thee* — Obadiah''s oracle against Edom; Herod''s planned violence against the Davidic infant continues the pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 3, 'numbers', 20, 14, 'Edom refusing passage to Yashar''el (Israel) at the wilderness border — the earliest beat of the Edom-against-Yashar''el pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 3, 'malachi', 1, 2, '*Yet I loved Ya''aqov (Jacob), and I hated Esau* — the divine-side reading of the long pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 3, 'ezekiel', 35, 1, 'The prophecy against Mount Seir for the perpetual hatred.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 3, 'psalms', 137, 7, '*Remember, O Yahuah (LORD), the children of Edom in the day of Yerushalayim (Jerusalem)* — the cry against Edom for joining the Babylonian destruction.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 16, 'genesis', 27, 41, '*And Esau hated Ya''aqov (Jacob) ... the days of mourning for my father are at hand; then will I slay my brother Ya''aqov (Jacob)* — Esau''s first attempted-murder of Ya''aqov (Jacob); Herod''s slaughter of the infants is the latest beat of the same hatred.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 15, 'hosea', 11, 1, '*When Yashar''el (Israel) was a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Egypt* — Yashar''el (Israel) as Yahuah''s (God''s) firstborn son brought out of Egypt at the Exodus; Matthew applies the verse to Yahusha (Jesus) as the embodiment of Yashar''el (Israel).'),
  ('matthew', 2, 13, 'exodus', 1, 8, 'Pharaoh''s order to kill the Hebrew male infants — the Tanakh-pattern of slaughter-of-the-infants-to-prevent-the-deliverer that Matthew 2:16 recapitulates with Herod-Yahusha (Jesus) in the lead roles.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 13, 'exodus', 2, 1, 'The preservation of the infant Mosheh (Moses) on the Nile while the other Hebrew infants were killed — the Tanakh-pattern of the deliverer preserved through the infant-slaughter.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 14, 'genesis', 46, 1, 'The patriarch Yoseph (Joseph) bringing Ya''aqov (Jacob) and his sons down to Egypt — the Tanakh-Yoseph initiating the Egypt-sojourn that the Matthew-Yoseph (Joseph) re-walks with the Messianic-Yashar''el (Israel) in his arms.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 14, 'exodus', 12, 40, 'The four-hundred-year Egypt-sojourn ended by the Exodus — the duration the Matthew-Egypt-sojourn telescopes into a few years for the Messiah, but recapitulates as the same pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 19, 'exodus', 4, 19, '*Go, return into Egypt: for all the men are dead which sought thy life* — the angelic-instruction to Mosheh (Moses) parallel to Matt 2:20''s angelic-instruction to Yoseph (Joseph): *they are dead which sought the young child''s life.* The verbal parallel is deliberate.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'jeremiah', 31, 15, 'The Rachel-weeping verse Matthew quotes.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'jeremiah', 31, 16, '*Refrain thy voice from weeping ... thy children shall come again to their own border* — the immediate prophetic answer to the weeping.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'jeremiah', 31, 31, 'The new-covenant promise — the deeper answer to the weeping, enacted in the blood of the Messianic child Matthew is protecting in the same chapter.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'genesis', 35, 16, 'Rachel''s death in childbirth near Beth-lehem (Ephrata) — the biographical anchor of the Rachel-weeps-for-children motif and the connection to the Beth-lehem geography of Matthew 2.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'jeremiah', 31, 9, '*I will cause them to walk by the rivers of waters in a straight way, wherein they shall not stumble: for I am a father to Yashar''el (Israel), and Ephraim is my firstborn* — the gathering of the northern house, which Rachel''s children (Yoseph (Joseph) and Binyamin (Benjamin)) are most associated with.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 18, 'matthew', 26, 28, '*For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins* — Yahusha (Jesus) enacting the Jer 31:31-34 new covenant in his blood at the Last Supper, twenty-six chapters after the Matt 2 infant-protection.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'isaiah', 11, 1, '*A Branch (netser) shall grow out of his roots* — the primary etymological connection; Natsareth (Nazareth) as *netser*-town.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'jeremiah', 23, 5, '*I will raise unto David a righteous Branch* (here *tsemach,* a different Branch-word but the same Messianic theme) — the broader prophetic Branch-tradition Matthew references with *the prophets* (plural).'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'jeremiah', 33, 15, '*In those days, and at that time, will I cause the Branch of righteousness to grow up unto David* — the parallel Branch-prophecy.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'zechariah', 3, 8, '*Behold, I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH* — Zechariah''s Branch-naming.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'zechariah', 6, 12, '*Behold the man whose name is The BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of his place* — Zechariah''s Branch-naming with the grow-up-out-of-his-place language that resonates with Matthew''s coming-out-of-Natsareth.'),
  ('matthew', 2, 23, 'isaiah', 53, 2, '*He shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness* — the despised-Branch reading that supplements the *netser* etymology.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 1, 'malachi', 4, 5, 'The Tanakh''s closing prophecy of Eliyahu (Elijah) sent before the great and dreadful day of Yahuah (the LORD) — the prophetic source Yochanan (John) embodies.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 1, '1-kings', 18, 1, 'Eliyahu (Elijah) at Mount Carmel confronting the Ba''al-system — the Tanakh-pattern of the wilderness-prophet calling the covenant people to choose.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 4, '2-kings', 1, 8, '*He was an hairy man, and girt with a girdle of leather about his loins* — Eliyahu''s (Elijah''s) garment, echoed in Yochanan''s (John''s) camel-hair and leather girdle.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'ezekiel', 18, 30, 'The prophetic-*teshuvah* call — *turn yourselves from all your transgressions ... cast away from you all your transgressions ... and make you a new heart* — the kind of repentance Yochanan (John) is calling for, not Reformation-style justification-by-faith-alone repentance.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 1, 'isaiah', 40, 3, 'The wilderness-voice preparing the way; opens Yeshayahu''s (Isaiah''s) gathering-and-return prophecies.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'matthew', 23, 33, 'Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) own *Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers* identification of the scribes and Pharisees — the same diagnostic Yochanan (John) named first.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'john', 8, 44, '*Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do* — the seed-war identification of the leadership-system.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'genesis', 3, 15, 'The Tanakh-source of the serpent-seed-vs-woman-seed enmity that the *vipers* identification draws on.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'acts', 15, 1, 'The first-century Judaizer-party — *certain men which came down from Yahudah (Judaea)* and the believing Pharisees demanding circumcision of Gentile believers — the apostolic-era continuation of the same system.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'galatians', 2, 4, '*False brethren unawares brought in, who came in privily to spy out our liberty which we have in Messiah (Christ) Yahusha (Jesus), that they might bring us into bondage* — Paul naming the Judaizer-pattern by the same diagnostic.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'philippians', 3, 2, '*Beware of dogs, beware of evil workers, beware of the concision* — Paul''s denunciation of the circumcision-party using language structurally parallel to Yochanan''s (John''s) *vipers.*'),
  ('matthew', 3, 7, 'john', 3, 1, 'Nicodemus the Pharisee coming to Yahusha (Jesus) by night — the individual Pharisee who turns, the framework''s victim-not-enemy posture applied.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 13, 'joshua', 3, 14, 'The Yarden (Jordan)-crossing under Yahoshua (Joshua) — the Tanakh-pattern the Matt 3 immersion recapitulates.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 13, 'joshua', 1, 1, 'The commissioning of Yahoshua (Joshua) to lead the entry — the first-leader pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 13, '2-kings', 2, 6, 'Eliyahu (Elijah) and Elisha at the Yarden (Jordan) — the prophetic-mantle-transfer at the same river; the framework reads the gospel''s choice of Yarden (Jordan) as deliberately echoing this prophetic-action history.'),
  ('matthew', 3, 13, '2-kings', 5, 14, 'Na''aman (Naaman) the Syrian dipping seven times in the Yarden (Jordan) and being cleansed — the Yarden (Jordan) as the river of prophetic-action cleansing.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 5, 'psalms', 91, 11, 'The verse the devil quoted, with the qualifier *to keep thee in all thy ways* (v.11) omitted in the devil''s citation.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 5, 'deuteronomy', 6, 16, 'The OVERRIDING Torah-word Yahusha (Jesus) brought into the conversation — the canon-harmonized response.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 5, '1-john', 2, 3, '*He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar* — the 1234-of-Truth filter that rules out any scripture-reading that voids the commandments; the meta-test that disqualifies the devil''s Psalm-91 misuse and every parallel misuse.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 5, 'matthew', 22, 29, '*Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of Elohim (God)* — Yahusha (Jesus) naming the Sadducees'' selective-scripture reading as the source of their error; the same diagnostic.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 5, '2-peter', 3, 16, '*Some things hard to be understood, which they that are unlearned and unstable wrest, as they do also the other scriptures, unto their own destruction* — the apostolic naming of the scripture-twisting pattern.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'daniel', 10, 13, 'The prince of Persia, the prince of Grecia — the principalities administering the world''s kingdoms in Daniel''s vision.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'daniel', 10, 20, 'The prince of Persia, the prince of Grecia — the principalities administering the world''s kingdoms in Daniel''s vision.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'ephesians', 6, 12, '*We wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world* — the apostolic naming of the present-age power-structure.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, '1-john', 5, 19, '*The whole world lieth in wickedness* — the present-age administration described.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'daniel', 7, 13, '*One like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven ... and there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him* — the Father''s-timing transfer of the everlasting kingdom that Yahusha (Jesus) waits for; the kaph-comparative preserved as incarnation-honoring.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'revelation', 11, 15, '*The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Messiah (Christ); and he shall reign for ever and ever* — the future consummation of the kingdom-transfer Yahusha (Jesus) refused to short-circuit.'),
  ('matthew', 4, 8, 'genesis', 3, 15, 'The original promise of the seed-of-the-woman bruising the serpent''s head — the cross is the bruise; the temptation to take the kingdoms without the cross is the temptation to skip the prophecy.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 17, 'isaiah', 8, 20, '*To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, it is because there is no light in them* — the prophetic-testimony that any teaching that contradicts the Torah and the testimony lacks the light; the Tanakh''s own anti-antinomian standard.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 18, 'isaiah', 40, 8, '*The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our Elohim (God) shall stand for ever* — the Torah-as-eternal-word standard; Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) *one jot or one tittle* declaration walks the same prophetic stream.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 18, 'psalms', 119, 89, '*For ever, O Yahuah (the LORD), thy word is settled in heaven* — the Tanakh''s standing-of-the-Torah affirmation.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 19, '1-john', 2, 3, 'The master filter; the 1234 of Truth.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 19, 'romans', 3, 31, '*Do we then make void the law through faith? Elohim (God) forbid: yea, we establish the law* — Paul''s own explicit denial of the antinomian misreading of his ministry; the Torah is established by faith, not voided.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 19, 'romans', 7, 12, '*Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — Paul''s positive affirmation of the Torah''s continuing-goodness.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 17, 'jeremiah', 31, 33, '*I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts* — the new-covenant promise that fills the Torah with its heart-substance; Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) *fulfil* at v.17 is the Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:33 work.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 17, 'ezekiel', 36, 26, '*A new heart also will I give you ... and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them* — the Spirit-empowered Torah-walking promise; the framework reading of the *fulfilled* Torah.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 17, 'hebrews', 8, 10, '*I will put my laws into their mind, and write them in their hearts* — the apostolic quotation of Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:33 applied to the new-covenant gathering.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 19, 'james', 2, 8, '*If ye fulfil the royal law according to the scripture, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself, ye do well ... whosoever shall keep the whole law, and yet offend in one point, he is guilty of all* — Ya''aqov''s (James''s) affirmation of the Torah''s continuing-binding force and the unity of its commandments.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 21, 'leviticus', 19, 17, '*Thou shalt not hate thy brother in thine heart* — the Torah''s heart-substance of the sixth commandment; the oral tradition stopped at the act, the Torah always taught the heart-root.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 27, 'exodus', 20, 17, '*Thou shalt not covet thy neighbour''s wife* — the tenth commandment, naming the heart-coveting that precedes the act of adultery; the Torah already named the heart-substance.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 31, 'genesis', 2, 24, '*Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh* — the original marriage-design Yahusha (Jesus) restores; Yahusha (Jesus) will explicitly cite this at Matt 19:4-9 as the framework against the Pharisees'' Devarim (Deuteronomy) 24:1 question.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 31, 'matthew', 19, 8, '*Mosheh (Moses) because of the hardness of your hearts suffered you to put away your wives: but from the beginning it was not so* — Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) explicit interpretation of Devarim (Deuteronomy) 24:1 as concession-to-hardness, not Torah-mandate-of-permission.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 33, 'numbers', 30, 2, '*If a man vow a vow unto Yahuah (the LORD), or swear an oath to bind his soul with a bond; he shall not break his word, he shall do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth* — the Torah''s binding-of-oaths standard; Yahusha (Jesus) does not abolish the oath-form but cuts the gradation-evasion-system the oral tradition built.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 33, 'matthew', 23, 16, 'Yahusha (Jesus) at Matt 23 indicts the same gradation-system explicitly — *whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor* — confirming that Matt 5:33-37 is correction of the oral-tradition apparatus, not abolition of all oath-taking.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 38, 'romans', 13, 3, '*Rulers are not a terror to good works ... he beareth not the sword in vain: for he is the minister of Elohim (God), a revenger to execute wrath upon him that doeth evil* — the apostolic confirmation that the judicial-sphere retains the sword and the *lex talionis* function; Matt 5:38-42 is personal-disciple ethic, not abolition of the judicial Torah.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 43, 'leviticus', 19, 18, '*Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself* — the Torah''s actual word, the part of the oral-tradition quote that IS in the Torah.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 43, 'leviticus', 19, 34, '*The stranger that dwelleth with you shall be unto you as one born among you, and thou shalt love him as thyself* — the Torah''s extension of the love-command to the stranger, the part the oral tradition had ignored.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 43, 'exodus', 23, 4, '*If thou meet thine enemy''s ox or his ass going astray, thou shalt surely bring it back to him again ... thou shalt surely help with him* — the Torah''s positive command toward the enemy; there is no *hate thine enemy* command anywhere in the Tanakh.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 43, 'proverbs', 25, 21, '*If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink* — the wisdom-stream''s love-of-enemy ethic; Paul quotes this directly at Romans 12:20.'),
  ('matthew', 5, 48, 'genesis', 17, 1, '*I am El Shaddai (the Almighty God); walk before me, and be thou perfect (tamim)* — the *tamim*-standard from the Torah; *teleios* at Matt 5:48 is the Greek translation of *tamim.*'),
  ('matthew', 5, 48, 'deuteronomy', 18, 13, '*Thou shalt be perfect (tamim) with Yahuah (the LORD) thy Elohim (God)* — the Torah''s direct command to *tamim*-walk; Yahusha (Jesus) restates the same command at the close of the antitheses.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'hosea', 7, 13, '*Though I have redeemed them, yet they have spoken lies against me* — the anchor verse for the grace-and-the-opportunity-that-can-be-lost teaching.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'ezekiel', 18, 24, '*When the righteous turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity ... all his righteousness that he hath done shall not be mentioned* — the righteous can fall away.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'ezekiel', 33, 12, '*The righteousness of the righteous shall not deliver him in the day of his transgression* — explicit naming of the conditional-continuation.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'exodus', 32, 33, '*Whosoever hath sinned against me, him will I blot out of my book* — names can be blotted out for lawlessness; the warning is to the wheat, not to the tares.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'psalms', 69, 28, '*Let them be blotted out of the book of the living* — the Psalmist''s invocation of the blotting-out architecture.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'hebrews', 10, 26, '*If we sin wilfully after that we have received the knowledge of the truth, there remaineth no more sacrifice for sins* — the apostolic warning that the redeemed who walk away forfeit the redemption.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, 'matthew', 7, 21, '*I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity* — Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) own naming of the forfeit at the close of the Sermon, addressed to those who invoked his name.'),
  ('matthew', 6, 14, '1-john', 1, 9, '*If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins* — the standing-receipt of forgiveness contingent on the confession-and-walking-in-light posture; Matt 6:14-15 names the kingdom-citizen''s forgiveness-extension as the parallel condition.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 21, '1-john', 2, 3, '*Hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments. He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar* — the master-filter; Matt 7:21-23 is the King''s own articulation of the same diagnostic.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 21, 'matthew', 12, 50, '*Whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother* — the doing-of-the-Father''s-will as the kingdom-family-identification criterion; same standard.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 21, 'matthew', 25, 31, 'The sheep-and-goats judgment scene — separated by what they DID, not what they said; the practical-walking diagnostic Matt 7:21 articulates in proposition.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 22, 'deuteronomy', 13, 1, '*If there arise among you a prophet, or a dreamer of dreams, and giveth thee a sign or a wonder, And the sign or the wonder come to pass ... thou shalt not hearken unto the words of that prophet* — the Tanakh false-prophet diagnostic; signs-and-wonders are not the proof; the Torah-fidelity is.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 22, 'deuteronomy', 18, 20, '*That prophet, which shall presume to speak a word in my name, which I have not commanded him to speak ... shall die* — the false-prophet-in-the-Name diagnostic.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 22, '2-corinthians', 11, 13, '*Such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of HaMashiach (Christ). And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* — the apostolic confirmation that supernatural-credentials can attend false ministers.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 23, 'ezekiel', 20, 37, '*I will purge out from among you the rebels, and them that transgress against me* — the post-harvest sifting language Matt 7:23''s *depart from me* echoes; the discrimination of the wheat after the gathering.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 23, 'psalms', 6, 8, '*Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for Yahuah (the LORD) hath heard the voice of my weeping* — David''s psalm-anchor of the *depart from me, workers of iniquity* formula Yahusha (Jesus) quotes verbatim.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 23, '2-thessalonians', 2, 7, '*For the mystery of iniquity (anomia, torahlessness) doth already work* — the apostolic naming of the *anomia* — the mystery of TORAHLESSNESS — operating in the present age.'),
  ('matthew', 7, 23, '1-john', 3, 4, '*Whosoever committeth sin transgresseth also the law: for sin is the transgression of the law (anomia)* — the apostolic-direct equation of sin with *anomia.*'),
  ('2-peter', 3, 15, 'romans', 10, 9, 'The confession-and-belief verses most-wrested by the institutional-Christian system into a verbal-confession-only entry-criterion.'),
  ('2-peter', 3, 15, 'romans', 3, 31, '*Do we then make void the law through faith? Elohim (God) forbid: yea, we establish the law* — Paul''s own counter to the antinomian-wrest.'),
  ('2-peter', 3, 15, 'romans', 7, 12, '*Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good* — Paul''s own affirmation of the Torah.'),
  ('2-peter', 3, 15, 'galatians', 5, 6, '*Faith which worketh by love* — the integration Paul names that the wresting collapses.'),
  ('2-peter', 3, 15, 'matthew', 7, 21, 'The King''s own statement that the verbal-confession without the walking is not the entry; reads against the wrested Paul; harmonizes with Paul read whole.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'leviticus', 14, 2, 'The Torah''s cleansing-of-the-leper procedure Yahusha (Jesus) directs the healed man to fulfill.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'luke', 17, 14, 'The second leper-episode in Luke; Yahusha (Jesus) again sends the cleansed to the priest.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'matthew', 5, 17, 'The Torah-affirming Sermon-on-the-Mount declaration the first-miracle illustrates in practice.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'matthew', 12, 9, 'The Shabbat-healing of the man with the withered hand — same heart-Torah-walking-in-practice pattern; the oral-tradition Shabbat-fence broken; the Torah''s mercy-substance preserved.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'mark', 7, 10, 'Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) explicit distinction between the Torah of Elohim (God) and the *tradition of men;* the heart-Torah affirmed, the oral-tradition distortions corrected.'),
  ('matthew', 8, 4, 'acts', 6, 7, '*A great company of the priests were obedient to the faith* — the eventual response of some priests to the testimony the leper-cleansings constituted.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'hosea', 6, 6, 'The direct Tanakh-source.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'matthew', 12, 7, 'Yahusha''s (Jesus''s) second citation of Hosea 6:6, in the Shabbat-controversy context.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, '1-samuel', 15, 22, '*To obey is better than sacrifice* — the first articulation of the obedience-over-sacrifice principle.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'psalms', 40, 6, '*Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; mine ears hast thou opened.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'psalms', 51, 16, '*Thou desirest not sacrifice ... a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim (God), thou wilt not despise.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'isaiah', 1, 11, '*To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? ... cease to do evil; learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'jeremiah', 7, 21, '*I spake not unto your fathers ... concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices: But this thing commanded I them, saying, Obey my voice.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'amos', 5, 21, '*I hate, I despise your feast days ... But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 13, 'micah', 6, 6, '*He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good ... to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy Elohim (God).*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'isaiah', 62, 5, '*As the bridegroom rejoiceth over the bride, so shall thy Elohim (God) rejoice over thee.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'hosea', 2, 19, 'The betrothal-restoration of divorced-Yashar''el (Israel).'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'isaiah', 54, 5, '*Thy Maker is thine husband; Yahuah Tseva''ot (the LORD of hosts) is his name.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'jeremiah', 3, 14, '*I am married unto you* — addressed to *backsliding children;* the bridegroom-substance over scattered-Yashar''el (Israel).'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'john', 3, 29, 'Yochanan (John) the Immerser''s bridegroom-and-friend-of-the-bridegroom self-identification.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'ephesians', 5, 25, 'The bridegroom-bride architecture extended to the King-and-the-assembly relationship in Paul''s covenant-restoration framing.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'revelation', 19, 7, 'The eschatological-wedding-of-the-Lamb.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 15, 'revelation', 21, 2, '*The holy city, new Yerushalayim (Jerusalem), coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, '2-samuel', 7, 12, 'The Davidic-covenant foundation.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'isaiah', 11, 1, '*A Branch shall grow out of his roots* — the Davidic-shoot prophecy.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'jeremiah', 23, 5, '*I will raise unto David a righteous Branch ... and this is his name whereby he shall be called, Yahuah Tsidkenu (THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS).*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'ezekiel', 34, 23, '*My servant David* as the Messianic-shepherd.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'ezekiel', 37, 24, '*David my servant shall be king over them ... and David my servant shall be their prince for ever.*'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'matthew', 15, 22, 'The Canaanite woman''s *Son of David, have mercy on me* — recognition by a marginalized woman in Hellenistic territory.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'matthew', 20, 30, 'The Yericho blind men''s *Son of David, have mercy on us* — recognition again from the blind on the road.'),
  ('matthew', 9, 27, 'matthew', 21, 9, 'The triumphal-entry crowds'' *Hosanna to the Son of David* — the moment the marginalized-recognition becomes the collective-acclamation.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'matthew', 19, 28, '*Ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar''el (Israel)* — the eschatological-promise that locks the twelve-apostle / twelve-tribe correspondence.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'luke', 22, 30, 'The parallel throne-promise at the last supper.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'revelation', 21, 14, '*The wall of the city had twelve foundations, and in them the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb* — the new-Yerushalayim''s structural-architecture carrying the apostolic-naming.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'revelation', 21, 12, '*Twelve gates, and at the gates twelve angels, and names written thereon, which are the names of the twelve tribes of the children of Yashar''el (Israel)* — the same architecture from the twelve-tribe-side.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'revelation', 7, 4, 'The 144,000 firstfruits sealed from the twelve tribes (12,000 from each tribe by name) — the gathering-architecture''s specific-witness.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 1, 'ezekiel', 47, 1, 'The millennial-twelve-tribe land-allotment Yechezk''el details in the restoration-vision.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 14, 'matthew', 7, 6, '*Cast not your pearls before swine* — the parallel discrimination-principle at the broader-pearl-level; the same disposition of not-wasting-substance-on-unworthy-receivers.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 14, 'matthew', 8, 34, 'The Gergesene townspeople asking the King to leave; the implicit-modeling of the response Matt 10:14 will codify.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 14, 'acts', 13, 51, 'Direct apostolic-application by Paul and Bar-Naba (Barnabas).'),
  ('matthew', 10, 14, 'acts', 18, 6, 'Paul at Corinth: *I am clean: from henceforth I will go unto the Gentiles* — the same shake-the-dust-off pattern at the synagogue-rejection.'),
  ('matthew', 10, 15, 'genesis', 19, 24, 'The Sodom-and-Gomorrah destruction-narrative.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'jeremiah', 6, 16, '*Ask for the old paths, where is the good way, and walk therein, and ye shall find rest for your souls* — the direct Tanakh-citation.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'isaiah', 28, 12, '*This is the rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest.*'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'matthew', 23, 4, 'The Pharisaic-burden the King''s-yoke contrasts against.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'acts', 15, 10, 'Kefa''s (Peter''s) apostolic-restatement.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'galatians', 1, 14, '*The traditions of my fathers* — Paul naming the Pharisaic-oral-tradition the kingdom-citizens are released from.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'jeremiah', 31, 33, 'The Torah-on-the-heart Tanakh-anchor — the substance of the King''s-yoke.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'ezekiel', 36, 26, 'The new-heart-and-new-spirit Tanakh-promise — the substance that makes the yoke easy.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, '1-john', 5, 3, '*His commandments are not grievous.*'),
  ('matthew', 11, 28, 'matthew', 5, 17, 'The load-bearing anti-antinomian declaration of the Sermon — the Torah Yahusha (Jesus) is yoking the disciples to is the Father''s-Torah-internalized.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'matthew', 28, 18, '*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* — the post-resurrection restatement of the *all things delivered* substance.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'john', 1, 18, '*No man hath seen Elohim (God) at any time; the only begotten Son ... he hath declared him* — the parallel revelation-economy statement.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'john', 5, 19, '*The Son can do nothing of himself, but what he seeth the Father do* — the Son''s-derived-substance from the Father.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'john', 14, 6, '*He that hath seen me hath seen the Father* — the Son-reveals-the-Father substance.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'john', 10, 30, '*I and my Father are one* — the relational-unity statement.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'john', 17, 1, 'The high-priestly-prayer''s Father-Son relational-architecture detailed.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, '1-corinthians', 8, 6, '*To us there is but one Elohim (God), the Father ... and one Lord Yahusha (Jesus) Messiah (Christ), by whom are all things* — Paul''s Father-Son framework statement.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'hebrews', 1, 1, '*Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son ... the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person* — the Hebrews-Christology in Father-Son framework.'),
  ('matthew', 11, 27, 'colossians', 1, 15, '*Who is the image of the invisible Elohim (God), the firstborn of every creature* — the Formless-Formed substance in Paul''s letter.'),
